      "expected": "Every link to the primary loses carrier at once, as on a real power loss. The MLAG secondary sees its peer port ether2 go down and reverts its MLAG bonds to its own LACP system ID (mlag-lacp-fallback=yes), so both traffic hosts renegotiate LACP, with brief loss. Each host drops its member to the primary on carrier loss, without waiting for the LACP short timeout. The secondary's edge MLAG bonds keep forwarding throughout.",
